{#
  THE REMINDER — a BODY, not a document.

  Same contract as `invitation.twig`, and for the same reason that file carries two
  hundred lines of scar tissue about: `OtpService::sendBranded()` passes what it is
  given to `brandWrap()`, the house shell. A whole `<html>` here would reach the
  inbox as two documents nested — two mastheads, two footers — and the admin
  preview would not show it, because a preview that renders the fragment alone is a
  preview of a message nobody receives.

  The shell already provides: the wordmark, the category chip ("Reminder"), the hero
  image, the footer, the unsubscribe link, the hidden preheader, and the 600px card
  on its paper ground. This file starts at the countdown and ends at the sign-off.

  ── WHY THE COUNTDOWN IS THE FIRST THING AND NOT THE DATE ───────────────────

  The invitation's job was to say WHEN, so its date panel is the loudest thing in
  it. A reminder is read by somebody who already knows when — they have the letter
  and the pass. What they do not know, at a glance, is how long they have left, and
  that is the entire reason this message exists. So "in 9 days" is set as the
  display object and the date sits under it as the supporting fact.

  Type comes from the shell's body cell: DM Sans, 15px, 1.65, ink-2 on white.
  Anything set here that the shell already sets is a second opinion that will drift.

  ── REBUILT 3 OCT 2026: THE HANDOFF'S LADDER, AND ACCENT'S COLOURS ──────────

  Deleted and written again from docs/handoff/inventory/_emails.md (owner, 3 Oct 2026).
  Type sits on REFERENCE §6.2's closed ladder (the 11px labels are 11.5; TypeScaleTest),
  in px, which is right for mail. Every colour is `c.<token>` — `Accent::mail()`, passed
  in by the sender under the handoff's own names — where this file used to type colours
  that were in no palette. The shell it lands in (`OtpService::brandWrap()`) was rebuilt
  to the same two rules the same day. The mono reference and the tracked labels keep
  their voice: those rules are for screens, and MonoAndCaseTest leaves mail out.
#}

<p style="margin:0 0 6px;font-family:'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;color:{{ c.ink }}">{{ salutation }} {{ name }},</p>

{# ── THE COUNTDOWN ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Gold, not emerald. Emerald is reserved for ACTION on this platform — the pass
   button below is the only thing in this message a reader is asked to press, and
   painting a second thing green would put two calls to action on one screen. #}
<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%"
       style="margin:0 0 20px;background:{{ c['gold-wash'] }};border-left:4px solid {{ c.gold }};border-radius:0 8px 8px 0">
  <tr>
    <td style="padding:18px 20px">
      <p style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:{{ c['gold-ink'] }}">{{ headline }}</p>
      <p style="margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif;font-size:26px;line-height:1.2;color:{{ c.ink }}">{{ countdown_up }}</p>
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:{{ c['gold-ink'] }}">
        <strong style="color:{{ c.ink }}">{{ when_day }} {{ when_date }}</strong><br>
        {# when_time comes from DisplayTime::showZoned(), which appends the zone itself —
           appending another here printed "19:00 WAT WAT". #}
        {{ when_time }}{% if where %} · {{ where }}{% endif %}
      </p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

{# ── THE LETTER ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   One paragraph per block, and the blocks come from the body as written — because
   in these letters the rhythm IS the argument. "It represents trust." is a
   paragraph on its own and has to stay one; run together with what follows it, the
   line stops being a claim and becomes a clause.

   `|nl2br` and not a second split: a single newline inside a block is a line break
   on purpose (the values list on day two is five short lines that must stay five
   short lines). Twig's nl2br escapes BEFORE it inserts the <br>, so operator text
   is safe here without a raw filter — which is the only reason this loop can render
   something an admin typed. #}
{% for p in paragraphs %}
  <p style="margin:0 0 {{ loop.last ? 22 : 14 }}px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.65;color:{{ c['ink-2'] }}">{{ p|nl2br }}</p>
{% endfor %}

{# ── THE PASS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The house button: the green pill used by the invitation, the nomination and the
   claim emails. VML behind it, because Outlook desktop draws a padded anchor with
   the background dropped — a bare text link where the only action is. #}
<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="margin:0 0 10px">
  <tr><td>
    <!--[if mso]>
    <v:roundrect xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" href="{{ id_url }}" style="height:46px;v-text-anchor:middle;width:236px" arcsize="50%" strokecolor="{{ c.green }}" fillcolor="{{ c.green }}">
      <w:anchorlock/>
      <center style="color:{{ c.surface }};font-family:'DM Sans',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:600">Open your pass</center>
    </v:roundrect>
    <![endif]-->
    <!--[if !mso]><!-->
    <a href="{{ id_url }}" style="display:inline-block;background:{{ c.green }};color:{{ c.surface }};text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:16px;padding:13px 26px;border-radius:999px">Open your pass</a>
    <!--<![endif]-->
  </td></tr>
</table>
<p style="margin:0 0 24px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:{{ c.soft }}">
  It is a live page, not a ticket — open it on your phone at the door. The formal
  invitation, with the letter attached, is in your inbox from when we first wrote.
</p>

{# ── THE ASK ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Their reference does two jobs: their identity at the door and the code their
   guests spend. Repeated here because a reminder that made somebody go and find
   the first email to get the code has failed at being a reminder.

   A hairline panel rather than a second tinted one: the gold band above is this
   message's accent, and two filled panels on a 600px card is a page with no
   hierarchy left. #}
<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%"
       style="margin:0 0 14px;border:1px solid {{ c.line }};border-radius:8px">
  <tr>
    <td style="padding:16px 20px">
      <p style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:{{ c.soft }}">Bring your people</p>
      <p style="margin:0 0 4px;font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace;font-size:19px;letter-spacing:2px;color:{{ c.ink }}">{{ reference }}</p>
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:{{ c.soft }}">{{ discount }}% off · up to {{ quota }} guests</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
<p style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;color:{{ c['ink-2'] }}">
  There is still time to share it with the people you want in the room. It takes
  {{ discount }}% off their tickets, for up to {{ quota }} of them{% if tier_line %}{{ tier_line }}{% endif %}.
</p>
{# The secondary action gets its own line. Left inline it lands mid-sentence and then
   wraps, so an underlined green link breaks across two lines in the middle of a
   paragraph — which reads as damage rather than as the second thing to do. #}
<p style="margin:0 0 26px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.65">
  <a href="{{ events_url }}" style="color:{{ c.green }};font-weight:600;text-decoration:underline">Send them to the tickets&nbsp;→</a>
</p>

<p style="margin:0 0 4px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.65;color:{{ c['ink-2'] }}">
  We are looking forward to having you with us.
</p>
{# Both halves of the sign-off come from the view. "With appreciation" belongs to the
   countdown letters and "With respect" to the ordinary reminder — one is a nudge from
   an organiser, the other is five letters asking somebody what they believe — and the
   name is whoever the organiser signs these as. #}
<p style="margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.65;color:{{ c.ink }}">
  {{ sign_off }},<br><strong style="font-weight:600">{{ team }}</strong>
</p>
